    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d546">

                <pb facs="1017" n="995" sameAs="frus:frus1950v05/pg995"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">684A.85/9–1050: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                            Embassy in Israel
                    </hi><anchor n="1" xml:id="d546-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi>
                        <lb/>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">niact</hi>
                        
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1950-09-10T19:00:00-04:00">September 10,
                            1950—7 p. m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>106. Please bring substance of Amman tel 58 Sep 9<anchor n="2" xml:id="d546-f2"/>
                    rptd you as 21, urgently to attention FonOff,
                    and state USG wld appreciate receiving info from
                    Israeli Govt on matter. Add that “USG, as friend
                    both Israel find Jordan and deeply concerned over any reports of circumstances
                    which might lead to outbreak of hostilities, disturbed by events described in
                    Jordan FonMin’s note. State that US rep Amman
                    being instructed urge Jordan Govt take no precipitate action, view desirability
                    full examination and report on situation by UN
                    reps in Palestine.<anchor n="3" xml:id="d546-f3"/> Say that USG, lacking detailed info on alleged incursion,
                    unable reach final conclusion on rights and wrongs of matter pending receipt of
                    report of UN reps. Add that, however, view
                    apparent explosive <pb facs="1018" n="996" xml:id="pg996"/> nature of situation
                    and urgent necessity prevent any outbreak of hostilities, particularly when
                    Israeli-Jordan talks about to take place in Special Comite, it is opinion USG that, if Israeli forces have made move
                    described in Jordan note, course of wisdom requires their withdrawal pending
                    full examination of circumstances.<anchor n="4" xml:id="d546-f4"/>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Acheson</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d546-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d546-f1-content">
                <p>This telegram was repeated to London, Amman, Jerusalem, and Paris.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d546-f2" n="2" xml:id="d546-f2-content">
                <p>Not printed; but see footnote 4, <hi rendition="#italic">supra</hi>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d546-f3" n="3" xml:id="d546-f3-content">
                <p>See telegram 42, <hi rendition="#italic">infra</hi>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d546-f4" n="4" xml:id="d546-f4-content">
                <p>Embassies London, on September 13, and Paris, on September 14, advised that the
                    British and French Foreign Offices were taking parallel action. (Telegrams 1559
                    and 1360, respectively, 684A.85/9–1350, /9–1450)</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
